          "page": "982",
          "section": "Simulation",
          "quote": "a microstructure model for the relevant alloy is needed to combine it with the simulation software to calculate the average grain size and the degree of recrystallization. The model used in this study is a Zehner-Hollomon-Type approach [ 2], in which the coef ﬁcients of the relevant equations were determined by isothermal upsetting tests combined with mi- crostructure investigations of the upset samples:",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "e49690ddcb0746b9:part:070"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "alloy_system_2",
      "name": "Alloy 706",
      "material_category": "Ni-based superalloy",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": "992",
          "section": "Abstract",
          "quote": "The development of equipment and technology makes it possible to manufacture a Ø2000 mm Alloy 706 disc 800 MN hydraulic press in China. Generally, high temperature or low strain rate is needed during the closed-die forging process to lower the requirement for press capacity; however, it will result in coarse unrecrystallized grains which are not beneﬁcial for mechanical properties.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "e49690ddcb0746b9:part:070"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
